# LiteRT team's focus models (LFM2.5 / MiniCPM) + DeepSeek-R1 on iPhone 17 Pro —
# the iOS leg of the model-agnostic demo (Pixel leg: lu-focus-litert-android.cells).
# Catalog entries pin the same litert-community artifacts as the Android leg
# (gpu-opt file where one is published); backend is the litert-lm iOS default (GPU Metal).
#
# LFM2.5 correction (2026-08-25, google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM#3129): the 08-24
# engine-create failure recorded here as a Metal/DUS runtime problem was THIS
# HARNESS's fault. The app derives max_num_tokens from the task (~650 at the
# protocol's ctx=672), below the file's largest exported prefill length
# (1024); the mismatch surfaces downstream as DYNAMIC_UPDATE_SLICE shape
# rejections and then a Metal half4*float4 shader error, which is what the
# 08-24 capture recorded (raw: results/raw/2026-08-24-iphone-demo-models/).
# With max_num_tokens >= 1024 the published file runs delegated. The cell
# below therefore runs at context-tokens=1024 — a disclosed budget deviation
# from the ctx=672 short-chat protocol (also stamped per run in
# contextTokensConfigured); the model card documents the same requirement.
ios litert-lm litert-community/DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-1.5B short-chat runs=3
ios litert-lm litert-community/LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct short-chat runs=4 context-tokens=1024
ios litert-lm litert-community/MiniCPM5-1B short-chat runs=3
